##DESCRIPTION
##  Statistics problem: confidence intervals
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Hypothesis tests)
## DBsection(Independent samples - t)
## Date(11/04/2012)
## Institution(UBC)
## Author(Djun Kim)
## Level(3)
## KEYWORDS('statistics', 'statistical inference', 'hypothesis test', 'p-value', 'interpretation')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',         'PGML.pl',
    'parserCheckboxList.pl', 'PGchoicemacros.pl',
    'parserMultiAnswer.pl',  'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context("Numeric");

$sig_level = list_random(90, 95, 99);
$diff      = 100 - $sig_level;
$lb        = random(-1, -0.2, 0.1);
$ub        = random( 2,  5,   0.1);

$cb = CheckboxList(
    [
        [
            "A two-sided two-sample test for a difference between the two "
                . "population means is not rejected at the $diff% significance level.",
            "A two-sided two-sample test for a difference between the two "
                . "population means is rejected at the $diff% significance level.",
            "A two-sided paired test for a difference between the two population "
                . "means is rejected at the $diff% significance level.",
            "A two-sided paired test for a difference between the two population "
                . "means is not rejected at the $diff% significance level."
        ],
        'None of the above.'
    ],
    [0],
    labels => 'ABC'
);

BEGIN_PGML
A [$sig_level]% confidence interval for the difference between the means of two independent populations is found to be [`([$lb],[$ub])`].

Which of the following statements is/are correct? _CHECK ALL THAT APPLY_.

[_]{$cb}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Because 0 is in the confidence interval, this means that 0 is a plausible solution and thus no difference.  This means that there are two possible answers. Because the statement was for the means of two *independent populations*, the only answer is [$cb].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT(); 